# Pin the public npm registry for the whole repository.
#
# The packages are published to registry.npmjs.org, and npm records the registry
# it resolved from as an absolute `resolved` URL inside package-lock.json. A
# machine-wide npmrc pointing at a mirror (e.g. registry.npmmirror.com) therefore
# leaks mirror URLs into the committed lockfiles, and GitHub Actions refuses to
# fetch them: `npm ci` fails with
#
#   npm error code EALLOWREMOTE
#   npm error Refusing to fetch "@standard-schema/spec@https://registry.npmmirror.com/..."
#
# Pinning the registry here keeps every lockfile resolving from the same source
# the packages ship to. `packages/dsh-hooks-ordering/.npmrc` does the same for
# that package's pnpm installs (pnpm also needs it for `pnpm publish`).
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
